+# Web Hangul font provenance
+
+This package uses the unmodified Noto Sans CJK SC Regular 2.004 original by the Noto Project Authors (Adobe and Google), under SIL Open Font License 1.1.
+
+- Source: https://github.com/notofonts/noto-cjk/blob/f8d157532fbfaeda587e826d4cd5b21a49186f7c/Sans/OTF/SimplifiedChinese/NotoSansCJKsc-Regular.otf
+- Source commit: f8d157532fbfaeda587e826d4cd5b21a49186f7c.
+- File: fonts/2c76254f6fc379fd/NotoSansCJKsc-Regular.otf; exactly 16,437,364 bytes.
+- SHA-256: 2c76254f6fc379fddfce0a7e84fb5385bb135d3e399294f6eeb6680d0365b74b.
+- Licence: fonts/2c76254f6fc379fd/OFL.txt, copied unchanged from the pinned source's Sans/LICENSE.
+- Font bytes are supplied at packaging time, never committed or subsetted. The source font name is unchanged.
+- The web shell fetches only the relative package path, with credentials omitted; it verifies the bytes locally before registering them for document text, the font menu, and every UI font family.
+- No CDN, external runtime service, host permissions or origin policy changes are required.
+
+Build with public PhotoCraft v0.9.0 source c699e3cda69f4852b43c0b191ab0091aaeff9d6a plus this patch. Preserve its original release source and dependency pins. Prepare a folder with fonts/manifest.txt copied from packaging/web/hangul-fonts-manifest.txt and the two original files at the paths above. Set PHOTOCRAFT_WEB_FONTS_DIR to that folder when running packaging/web/package.sh. Set PHOTOCRAFT_HANGUL_FONT to the original OTF when running the required ignored regression test:
+
+    cargo test --locked -p photocraft-ui-egui hangul_font::tests -- --include-ignored
+
+The regression test checks the pinned SHA-256, every modern Hangul syllable U+AC00 through U+D7A3 through the application's skrifa cmap reader, the menu family, egui glyphs, and UI font reinstallation. Browser rendering, IME, saved-document reopen and exports require separate runtime verification.
